  "term": "trisomy 21",
  "definition": "Trisomy 21 is a genetic condition in which chromosome 21 is present in extra full or partial form. It is linked with a recognizable pattern of physical differences, moderate to severe intellectual disability, and higher rates of heart and digestive abnormalities, leukemia, and unusually early Alzheimer-type brain disease.",
